  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan lists Doctor Su Shou with Roaming Doctor Jiu Zhi, Doctor Sheng Shou, and Doctor Sha Ren when he points Bai Ning Bing toward treatment in Shang clan city.",
      "chapters": [
        271
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_doctor_su_shou",
        "char_travelling_doctor_jiu_zhi",
        "char_bai_ning_bing",
        "loc_shang_clan_city"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later roster names the four as killer ghost doctor Chou Jiu, doctor Su Shou, travelling doctor Jiu Zhi, and divine doctor Sheng Shou.",
      "chapters": [
        375
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "four-doctors-roster",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_chou_jiu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In Fang Yuan’s prior life memory, only after Shang Yan Fei invited Doctor Su Shou together with Divine Doctor Sheng Shou did they suppress Chou Jiu’s glamor at Yi Tian mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        383
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "prior-life-memory-of-yi-tian",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_shang_yan_fei",
        "loc_yi_tian_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan groups the four great doctors’ peculiarities and notes that Divine Doctor Sheng Shou is a male who likes other males.",
      "chapters": [
        385
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "treatment-of-wu-shen-tong",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wu Shen Tong goes to him after Long Qing Tian’s jade sky Gu poison. Divine Doctor Sheng Shou touches his chest, says he came too late, that the poison has seeped into bone marrow, that life and cultivation can be preserved, that the poison cannot be removed, and that regular detox visits will be needed.",
      "chapters": [
        386
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "treatment-of-wu-shen-tong",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_wu_shen_tong",
        "char_long_qing_tian",
        "gu_jade_sky_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At that war he supports the righteous path: with his healing, righteous path Gu Masters take fewer losses and recover injuries quickly enough to fight hard. Xiao Shan uses a surface attack as a diversion while sending Lu Zuan Feng to sneak in and kill him; the attempt fails, and Shang Fu Xi ambushes and kills Second Zombie King instead. Chou Jiu’s arrival then suppresses him until Shang clan sends Doctor Su Shou, and the two together close the gap Chou Jiu opened.",
      "chapters": [
        966
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "yi-tian-mountain-war",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "char_xiao_shan",
        "char_lu_zuan_feng",
        "char_shang_fu_xi",
        "char_second_zombie_king",
        "fac_shang_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At Wu clan, among over fifty Gu Masters gathered for immortal ascension support, Divine Doctor Sheng Shou and Wu Shen Tong are two revived through the dead sea life retrieval formation.",
      "chapters": [
        2132
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wu-clan-immortal-ascension-cohort",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
